<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Europe</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Europe is the western part of the Eurasian landmass. It was the home of empires such as the Roman, Carolingian, Holy Roman and Austro-Hungarian, and from the fifteenth century European states built overseas empires that reached the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>. Through trade, conquest and diplomacy, Europe figures in the histories of almost every empire covered by the site, from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/europe.jpg" alt="Europe" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rob984 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Europe_orthographic_Caucasus_Urals_boundary_(with_borders).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
